Q: Changing locale dynamically in Vue app doesn&#39;t update translated values on pages A: <p>If you mean the <code>label: i18n.t(...)</code>, it will only run once. Any changes in language will not change the label. One solution is to put the text keys in your fields and use $t in your component on the variable containing the text key:</p>
<p><code>field.js</code></p>
<pre><code>...
const fields = {
  userId: {
    label: 'users.generalInfo.userId',
...
</code></pre>
<p><code>component</code></p>
<pre><code>&lt;v-text-field 
  :label=&quot;$t(fields.userId.label)&quot;
/&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Border around elements with new WordPress 7.0 update A: <p>This is probably caused by Avada's post-rendering JavaScript, because only when you remove the border color does it go back to normal. The style is --awb-border-color and I have no clue why it does this, but I ran into it today too.</p>
<p>Add this inside of Avada Global Options, CSS:</p>
<pre><code>[style*=&quot;--awb-border-color&quot;] {
    border: none !important; 
}
</code></pre>

Q: Passing user id to PostgreSQL triggers A: <p>I implemented a wrapper for TransactionManager, a config to use the transaction manager and SET LOCAL/set_config.</p>
<p>I have used the request context, but it is possible use a thread local context for it.</p>
<p>In your request security interceptor:</p>
<p><code>request.setAttribute(&quot;USER_ID&quot;, user.getId());</code></p>
<pre><code>public class PostgresSessionTransactionManager extends JpaTransactionManager {

    @PersistenceContext
    private EntityManager entityManager;

    @Override
    protected void doBegin(
        Object transaction,
        TransactionDefinition definition
    ) {
        super.doBegin(transaction, definition);

        ServletRequestAttributes attributes =
            (ServletRequestAttributes) RequestContextHolder.getRequestAttributes();

        if (attributes != null) {
            HttpServletRequest request = attributes.getRequest();
            Object uidAttribute = request.getAttribute(&quot;USER_ID&quot;);

            if (uidAttribute != null) {
                String userId = uidAttribute.toString();
                entityManager
                .createNativeQuery(
                    &quot;SELECT set_config('app.user_id', :userId, true)&quot;
                )
                .setParameter(&quot;userId&quot; userId)
                .getSingleResult();
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>The transaction configuration to wrap the transaction manager bean in <code>@Transactional</code>:</p>
<pre><code>@Configuration
@Slf4j
public class TransactionManagerConfig {

    @Bean
    @Primary
    public PlatformTransactionManager transactionManager(
        EntityManagerFactory entityManagerFactory
    ) {
        PostgresSessionTransactionManager txManager =
            new PostgresSessionTransactionManager();
        txManager.setEntityManagerFactory(entityManagerFactory);
        return txManager;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>In PostgreSQL, triggers and descendant transactions will be available to the <code>app.user_id</code> configuration using <code>current_setting('app.user_id', true)</code>.</p>
